export anchor TimelineFirstStyle:
    number: 181
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Timeline first
    idea: A blue-grey planning view where the projects are the hero as bars on a September to January date axis, cut by a today line at 31 October, with a slim KPI band above and the chart and activity below.
    base: light
    palette:
        page: #f1f4f7, the page
        band: #e3e9ef, the header band
        surface: #ffffff, the timeline, panels and fields
        past: #e9eef3, the shaded time before today and row rules
        ink: #1a2632, text, the today line and its label
        muted: #4c5d6e, labels, dates and axis months
        line: #d3dce5, borders and dashed month lines
        steel: #2f5d86, the primary button, this week bars, the avatar and focus
        steelDeep: #244a6c, links and the current nav text
        steelSoft: #7a8fa6, last week bars, KPI rules and field edges
        greenBar: #cfe3d6, On track bars, with #22683e for the word and shape
        amberBar: #f0dfc2, At risk bars, with #875200 for the word and shape
        redBar: #f2d2cd, Behind bars, with #ad2a1f for the word, shape and overdue
    type:
        One stack, Avenir Next, Segoe UI, Helvetica Neue, system-ui,
        Roboto, Arial. KPI figures 28px at 600, the greeting 24px at 650,
        panel titles 16px at 650, project names 14px at 650, axis months
        and the column label 12px at 650, notes 12 to 13px.
    layout:
        A blue-grey band spans the top. Its first row has a three bar
        stepped mark with the brand at left, the six nav links centred as
        text with Home in a white tab, and a bell, a square steel avatar and
        Mara Okafor at right. Its second row has the greeting with the date
        and a red clock with 4 tasks are overdue at left, and the search
        field and a steel New project button at right. Below the band four
        KPIs sit in one row without boxes, each a figure over its label
        behind a 3px left rule, the overdue rule and figure in red. The
        timeline panel follows across the full width. Its axis row has a
        250px Project column label then the months Sep 2026, Oct, Nov, Dec
        and Jan 2027 placed by date, with a dark Today 31 Oct tag. Each of
        the six rows, sorted by days left, has a label cell with name, team,
        percent, tasks and the status word with shape, and a lane where the
        time before today is shaded, dashed month lines run down, a solid
        dark today line cuts through, and a status tinted bar runs from
        today to the due date, ending in the filled status shape with the
        due date and days left beneath. A footnote names the nearest and
        furthest due dates. Below, two panels side by side, Tasks completed
        as seven weekday pairs of bars, last week beside this week, and
        Activity as rows of time then sentence. Below 1000px the nav wraps
        to its own row and the lower panels stack. Below 720px each project
        label sits above its lane, the axis keeps all five months at phone
        width and the KPIs become two by two.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 20px panel padding, 72px timeline rows, 20px between panels, 32px page gutter.
    density: Medium. One project per lane, read left to right through time.
    corners: 8px panels, 6px controls, tabs and avatar, 4px bars.
    borders: 1px #d3dce5 panels, dashed month lines, a 2px ink today line, 3px left rules on KPIs.
    shadows: One faint 0 1px 2px at 5 percent ink on the timeline panel only.
    icons:
        Line icons at 1.8px stroke at text size. Filled status shapes mark
        each bar end and the label cell, a check circle for On track, a
        triangle with a bang for At risk and a crossed square for Behind,
        plus a clock ring for overdue.
    focus: A 2px steel outline offset 2px with a 5px pale steel halo.
    tone: Calm planning language built on dates and days left, such as 20 Nov, 20 d.
